Helios patch 0002 fuel-counter (Luau 0.739; 02 §7.4, 04 §10.2; WP-0.10r, K39)

Helios charges one fuel per gc < 0 `interrupt` safepoint (loop back edges, calls, returns, pattern-matcher
steps). Calling the host's interrupt at every safepoint cost 12-17 % of script time against RT-13's
<= 10 %. This patch puts an inline counter (global_State::fuelcounter, reached through the new
lua_fuelcounter) in front of every gc < 0 interrupt call, in the interpreter (VM_INTERRUPT), the pattern
matcher and native code (x64 and A64 INTERRUPT lowering and the shared interrupt helper): the safepoint
decrements the counter and calls interrupt only when the result is <= 0, after resetting it to 0. The host
arms the counter with the fuel left until its next decision point (kill, soft budget, wall-clock read), so
it is called only there and counts exactly the same fuel. The counter starts at 0, so a host that never
arms it keeps stock behaviour (interrupt at every safepoint). GC-step interrupts (gc >= 0) are unchanged.
The host can also subtract charges from the counter (binding and builtin fuel costs).

Upstream status: not submitted. Rebase on every Luau bump (K10): every caller of cb.interrupt with
gc < 0 must go through the counter. Licence: MIT (Helios, like Luau).

